    #t9dRkDy6ubuv6VSbtek7E9ns ^"Weight of Common Materials" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Character"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Table Columns" LIST ["Material", "Weight of 1 ft3", "Number of ft3*"]
            ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
        }
        TABLE {
            "Beer or wine" "64 lb" "6"
            "Dirt" "94 lb" "270"
            "Gemstone" "235 lb" "6/10000**"
            "Gold" "1180 lb" "1/10***"
            "Iron" "490 lb" "1"
            "Fresh leaves or vegetation" "20 lbs" "27"
            "Olive oil" "57 lb" "62"
            "Silver" "655 lb" "1/10***"
            "Stone" "155 lb" "27"
            "Water" "62 lb" "622"
            "Wheat" "50 lb" "27"
            "Wood" "37 lb" "27"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "* in Target: Individual 1728 Individuals in a cubic foot *** 10 Individuals in a cubic foot

For humans and animals, the Size characteristic is a good indicator of weight. A +1 increase in Size doubles the weight, +2 points of Size is a fivefold increase in weight, and +3 points of Size is a tenfold increase. The inverse is true when reducing points of Size."
    }
