        }
        PERSONALITY_TRAITS {
            "Uncertain Faith" +1
            "Good Listener"
            "Compassionate"
            "Duty-Bound"
            "Strict"
        }
        CHOICES {
            CHOICE [^"Priest" NOTE "Christian Confessor", ^"Relic" SIZE "Minor" NOTE "Christian Confessor", "'Alim", ^"Educated" OF "Islamic" SIZE "Minor" NOTE "Islamic Confessor", "Rabbi", ^"Educated" OF "Hebrew" SIZE "Minor" NOTE "Jewish Confessor"]
            CHOICE [^"Vow" OF "Celibacy" SIZE "Major" NOTE "Christian Confessor", ^"Weakness" OF "Drinking" SIZE "Minor" NOTE "Christian Confessor", ^"Vow" OF "Celibacy" SIZE "Major" NOTE "Islamic Confessor", ^"Temperate" NOTE "Islamic Confessor", ^"Outsider" SIZE "Minor" NOTE "Jewish Confessor", ^"Meddler" SIZE "Minor" NOTE "Jewish Confessor"]
            CHOICE [^"Student", ^"Churchman", ^"Covenfolk", ^"Local", ^"Leader", ^"Public Official"]
        }
        NOTES {
            "Age and Characteristics" "The Confessor may be anyone from an inexperienced young priest, through a mature monk, to an elderly imam. But he tends to have high Intelligence, Communication, and Presence characteristics. There is an opportunity to build long relationships between a younger Confessor and the magi of the covenant, and see those relationships grow throughout the saga. The character can be used by the storyguide to confront characters with their actions, and help the players explore their consequences."
            "Suggested Abilities" "Aside from knowledge of Latin, the Artes Liberales, the Church, and Theology, the Confessor relies upon his Folk Ken for gaining an intuition of what troubles his flock, Leadership to maintain his position as a pillar of the community, and various Lores for his village, the covenant, and the local area to keep abreast of all the current events."
            "Personality Traits" "If the Confessor has taken the new Uncertain Faith Flaw, he has a Personality Trait of the same name with a score of at least 1. As for other traits, he is likely to be a Good Listener, which helps further define his role in the saga. A third trait says more about the Confessor as a person, who may be Compassionate, Duty-Bound, or Strict."
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This is not the first time we have discussed these matters, maga Umbra, and I fear it shall not be the last.

A magus' soul is imperiled just as much, if not more so, by temptation and obsession as any person's. The abstract allure of knowledge and power provide new opportunities for sin to take hold and guide the magus away from the righteous path. So it is important for the magus to make peace with his maker and be absolved of sin. This is where the Confessor comes in.

Every community has a need to find resolution for things that prey heavily upon the conscience. Christian tradition has the sacrament of penance and the practice of confession at its heart. In confessing his sins to a priest and undertaking the prescribed penance, a character's soul is cleansed, and the character is free to resume his life unencumbered by sin. This is one of the key roles played by the priest in his community.

Covenants are often similar to manorial holdings in that they rely on one or more villages not only for income, but also for their day-to-day activities. The covenant is also home to servants, cooks, guards, librarians, and all manner of other covenfolk. These communities, both inside and outside of the covenant, need spiritual guidance.

The Confessor is a priest or religious leader who provides confidential counsel and moral guidance to those in his parish. In the case of a Christian priest, the receiving of confession is a responsibility of his office and a duty to his parishioner's soul. Even if the Confessor doesn't live within the covenant, he lives nearby and receives the visits of magi, just as he would others in his parish.

The Confessor is also well-placed to act on behalf of the magi in matters concerning the Church, and may find himself drafted into service from time to time."
    }
    #thfiCZ6reFxOUgXUJecmKc1O TEMPLATE "The Corpse-Thief" DEF {
