        EXTENDS #tgA0K9vGShU1WKTibhCc4jXz ^"Flaw"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor" FIXED
            ^"Category" STRING "Personality" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The character is a follower, not a leader. He rarely takes the initiative, but is usually happy to follow the direction of a forthright and decisive person. If he finds a leader, he tends to stick with him."
    }
    #tPN6kzMdU3Cd8BermHAd9Lb0 ^"Stuck in His Ways" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tgA0K9vGShU1WKTibhCc4jXz ^"Flaw"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor" FIXED
            ^"Category" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Having come from a covenant, this character knows how things must be done to best serve the needs of covenfolk and magi alike. Only, his new home does things differently. And they're wrong. When making Stress Rolls against his Profession Abilities or any Ability concerning his new covenant, such as Leadership or Folk Ken, this character uses the lower of that Ability score and his current Covenant Lore Ability for his current covenant. Note that bonuses from Puissance or other Virtues still apply to the roll.

This Flaw can also be applied to organizations other than covenants, such as abbeys, universities, guilds, or churches."
        REFERENCES {
            "Folk Ken" -> #tsjid9PuuYMjxSZew5KRo08D ^"Folk Ken"
        }
    }
    #t3D2Jc3McklTo6ZIB9Str0EQ ^"Susceptible to Warping" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tgA0K9vGShU1WKTibhCc4jXz ^"Flaw"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor" FIXED
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Your character's constant exposure to magic at the side of his magus has made him more susceptible to supernatural Warping than he might otherwise be.

In any year in which the character gains a Warping Point from any Realm or any source (including Longevity Rituals, living within an aura, and powerful supernatural effects), the character gains one additional Warping Point associated with that same Realm. This means that if he gains a single Warping Point from each Realm in a year, he gains four additional Warping Points, one from each Realm, at the end of that year.

These additional points do not contribute to Wizard's Twilight or to other events caused by the acquisition of Warping Points as they accrete slowly over the course of the year."
        REFERENCES {
            "Longevity Rituals" -> #tExlPnQFFU4L9wpE5R5J52SL ^"Longevity Rituals"
            "Wizard's Twilight" -> #tGwT43yDXxcBX5sJJVrbSBMH ^"Wizard's Twilight"
        }
    }
    #tBEAfwKP1OjBLJg2WXs6Gsij ^"Worthless Abilities" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tgA0K9vGShU1WKTibhCc4jXz ^"Flaw"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor" FIXED
            ^"Category" STRING "General" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A time-lost character (see Chapter 7: Grog Templates) must have about 30 experience points that have been rendered valueless by her shift in time. For example, she may have Area Lore of 3 for a city that no longer exists, or her Etiquette score may have been rendered useless by changing social structures. Troupes may permit companions to purchase this Flaw multiple times.

In the example of the legionaries given in the Time-lost Witnesses template (see Chapter 7), their wasted ability is their Organization Lore. The army to which it refers no longer exists."
    }
    # ^"Master of (Form) Creatures" — Grogs reprints this Virtue but
    # miscategorises it as Minor, General. It originates in Realms of
    # Power: Magic as Minor, Supernatural — the one canonical anchor is
    # #tG6mBUvvNcf2QegjbxOSpAx6 in arm5e-rop-magic-0.5-virtues-flaws.
    # Per the cross-book ownership rule the originating book owns the
    # canonical DEF; Grogs references it (see the Gryphon Trainer entry
    # in arm5e-grogs-0.5-templates, which DEPENDS_ON the RoP:Magic V&F
    # module) rather than redefining it. Grogs' erroneous General
    # category is dropped (owner ruling, 2026-07-26).
    #trjUvwxOmVyB9s4cIuNcQ21N ^"Mythic Farrier" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor" FIXED
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Grogs"
        }
        FORMULAS {
            "Craft Total" "controlling Characteristic (Intelligence or Dexterity) + Craft: Farrier"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The character may use the Touched by (Realm) Virtue (*City &* *Guild*, page 71), to a limited extent. He may craft horseshoes with magical effects, using Hermetic guidelines for a single Hermetic Form, chosen at character creation. Animal is a popular choice. The powers of the horseshoes can only affect the horse itself, or its immediate environment. A Terram effect, for instance, to make the ground which the horse touches stable is permissible, but an Auram power to change the weather isn't. To calculate the Craft Total, add the controlling characteristic to the Craft: Farrier Ability. As this field of work requires wit as well as deftness of hand, either Intelligence or Dexterity may be used; this is a permanent choice which must be made at character creation. This ability is most likely aligned with the Magical or Faerie Realm, but an Infernal farrier is a possibility. You may take this Virtue twice, but no more. Taking the Virtue a second time adds either a second Form to use while enchanting, or allows the character to use it with another Ability, but not both. For variations on this Virtue, simply rename it Mythic (Professional), and replace Craft: Farrier with another Craft Ability. Retain the limit of a single Ability and a single Hermetic Form."
        REFERENCES {
            "Hermetic Form" -> #tUEdmiz0IADMNt9MPAbcgRyn ^"Hermetic Form"
            "Craft: Farrier" -> #tdxESVednr2TuKq8LcQQ5Bga ^"Craft: Farrier"
            "Craft: Farrier" -> #tdxESVednr2TuKq8LcQQ5Bga ^"Craft: Farrier"
            "Hermetic Form" -> #tUEdmiz0IADMNt9MPAbcgRyn ^"Hermetic Form"
        }
    }
    #t198c5d4aebea9b31d3968a ^"Pack Leader / Natural Leader" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor"
            ^"Category" STRING "General"
            ^"Source" STRING "Houses of Hermes: Mystery Cults"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The character is a dominant person with a demeanor that encourages others to do what he says. His self-assured manner gives him a +3 bonus to social situations

in which he takes the lead; people are more likely to follow his orders or do as

he suggests. If he is Gifted, this bonus can temporarily help to overcome the social

penalty of The Gift, due to the strength of his domineering personality. Members of House Bjornaer who were Initiated early in their apprenticeship often have this Virtue."
    }
    # Hedge Magic [Revised Edition] is an EXTENSION on the arm5e edition, loaded
    # alongside the core rulebook (spec S13 composition). It declares the types
    # the supplement introduces that the core rulebook has no place for: the
    # magic systems of the six hedge traditions.
    # 
    # What it does NOT declare, deliberately:
    # - Virtues and Flaws. The book's 101 hedge Virtues and Flaws fit the core
    # ^"Virtue"/^"Flaw" types unchanged (same Size enum, same free-text
    # Category axis), so armdef-hedge-magic-0.5-virtues-flaws.ttrpg EXTENDS
    # ^"Virtue"/^"Flaw" and DEPENDS_ON ArM5_Core_Virtue_Flaw directly. The
    # four entries the book prints as "New or Revised" that share a name with
    # a core Virtue/Flaw (Elemental Magic, Fast Caster, Slow Caster,
    # Secondary Insight) are emitted as MODIFY of the core anchor with a
    # verbatim "Hedge Magic Note" — never a second DEF of the same name —
    # exactly as Realms of Power: Magic revises core Virtues/Flaws.
    # ---------------------------------------------------------- Hedge Arts
    # The hedge traditions that use an Art-and-form magic (Elementalists,
    # Gruagachan, Learned Magicians) each have their own Techniques and Forms,
    # parallel to (but distinct from) the Hermetic Arts. Twenty in all. Each is
    # a Technique or a Form of exactly one tradition.
    #t7873812fa0422bdd45a168 ^"Hedge Art" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Tradition" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Art Kind" ENUM ["Technique", "Form"] REQUIRED
            ^"Source" STRING DEFAULT "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A Technique or Form of a hedge tradition's Art-based magic (Elementalist, Gruagach, or Learned Magician), parallel to the Hermetic Arts but belonging to a single tradition."
        REFERENCES {
            "Hermetic Arts" -> #tdca161a54c8c70f3df81 ^"Hermetic Arts"
        }
    }
    # --------------------------------------------------------- Hedge Spells
    # The named spells of the hedge traditions, plus the new Hermetic spells the
    # book introduces for interacting with hedge magic. 57 in all. Each states
    # its tradition, its Technique and Form (as that tradition names them — the
    # Hermetic ones use Creo/Corpus, the Learned Magicians use Tueor/Fortunam,
    # the Gruagachan use Give/Blessing), a level, and a Range/Duration/Target
    # line. Range/Duration/Target are STRING, not the Hermetic enum: Gruagach
    # spells use Ranges like "Conversation" and Durations like "Limit"/"Geas".
    #t0366dd9f2578b0f22f9bc5 ^"Hedge Spell" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Tradition" ENUM ["Hermetic", "Learned Magicians", "Gruagachan"] REQUIRED
            ^"Technique" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Form" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Level" INTEGER MIN 1
            ^"Range" STRING
            ^"Duration" STRING
            ^"Target" STRING
            ^"Requisite" STRING
            ^"Code" STRING
            ^"Source" STRING DEFAULT "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A named spell of a hedge tradition (or a new Hermetic spell for interacting with hedge magic), with its tradition, Technique, Form, level, and Range/Duration/Target line."
    }
    # ---------------------------------------------------------- Rune Spells
    # The Vitkir cast by carving rune scripts. Each rune spell is inscribed with
    # a primary rune (optionally a secondary rune), has a level (a number, or
    # "General"), and uses one of the casting Methods. 48 in all.
    #t096cdf4e33c68fb634c969 ^"Rune Spell" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Rune" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Secondary Rune" STRING
            ^"Level" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Method" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Descriptor" STRING
            ^"Source" STRING DEFAULT "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A Vitkir rune spell, cast by carving a rune script. Inscribed with a primary rune (and optionally a secondary rune), at a level (numeric or General), using one of the casting Methods."
    }
    # --------------------------------------------------------------- Runes
    # The 24 runes of the Elder Futhark, each an h3 section of Chapter Seven with
    # its own letter, meaning, aett, and the kinds of effect it governs. The
    # rune's guideline write-up is its verbatim DESCRIPTION.
    #t52a8aa740f9b19b3496eb0 ^"Rune" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Letter" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Meaning" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Effects" STRING
            ^"Aett" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Source" STRING DEFAULT "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "One of the 24 runes of the Elder Futhark, with its Latin-letter transliteration, meaning, aett, and the kinds of magical effect it governs."
    }
    # ------------------------------------------------------- Modified Runes
    # The alternate-alphabet correspondences (The Anglo-Saxon Futhorc, The
    # Younger Futhark) the book tabulates for the Hermetic integration of rune
    # magic. 49 rows. These are pure alphabet-correspondence data — the book
    # gives no rules prose for them — so they are soft-statted from the table
    # (name, letter, pronunciation, meaning, Elder-Futhark equivalent).
    #tda5890a44fc8c7bf6e6533 ^"Modified Rune" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Table" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Letter" STRING
            ^"Rune Name" STRING REQUIRED
            ^"Pronounced" STRING
            ^"Meaning" STRING
            ^"Elder Equivalent" STRING
            ^"Source" STRING DEFAULT "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A rune from an alternate alphabet (the Anglo-Saxon Futhorc or the Younger Futhark) that the book tabulates against the Elder Futhark for Hermetic integration."
    }
    #tNSieg5eFwZruHMjUUnW1pg3 ^"Elementalist Air" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tT28cb9EpHcSa3Joedekm2A3 ^"Virtue"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Size" STRING "Minor" FIXED
            ^"Category" STRING "Supernatural" FIXED
            ^"Source" STRING "Hedge Magic [Revised Edition]"
        }
        FORMULAS {
            "Sanguine Personality Trait" "Warping Score + (Elementalist Air / 5)"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This power combines with the Elementalist Techniques to affect the element of air. Taking this Virtue gives the character an initial score of 0 in Elementalist Air (see Elementalist Forms, below), and a Sanguine Personality Trait (see Elemental Warping, below) equal to his Warping Score + (Elementalist Air / 5)."
        REFERENCES {
            "Personality Trait" -> #tcBZnRedWJ5vEcmMkio8kULU ^"Personality Trait"
        }
    }
