    # The chapter's weaknesses, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.
    #t18b41c29018d5b8c1ab087 ^"Abhorrent Material/Circumstance" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t0fa5697338cf5051460713 ^"Demon Weakness"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 33
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The demon cannot abide a particular type of object or substance, or a particular circumstance. This may be a common material such as light, salt, or garlic (for weak demons); or a reasonably uncommon, such as iron horseshoes, objects that have been given names, or charms made of rowan wood, for the more powerful demons. The material or circumstance inflicts no actual damage, but should such a thing come into the demon’s presence, the demon must flee, or else spend a Confidence Point to remain for two minutes. If it is unable to do either, then a brave or foolhardy soul may be able to strike a bargain with the demon using the advantage he has gained. A demon in the presence of its Abhorrent Material or Circumstance cannot regain spent Might Points. This weakness affects demons in both spiritual and physical form, but demons possessing a human are more resistant to their weaknesses, and may make a Stamina roll against an Ease Factor of 6 to remain in the presence of the abhorred material. If the roll is failed, the demon must either make its host flee, or if this is not possible, end the possession and flee itself."
    }
    #tcfa1a30b90b0d37069f911 ^"Compulsiveness" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t0fa5697338cf5051460713 ^"Demon Weakness"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 33
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The demon is compelled to enumerate randomly scattered objects; if, for example, a jar of beans is strewn in the path of this demon, it must count every one before it can proceed. The objects must be purposefully scattered in sight of the demon to hinder it."
    }
    #t9e651c6f92ba3cdad8335b ^"Ordering" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t0fa5697338cf5051460713 ^"Demon Weakness"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 33
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The demon has no power over anything that is sealed, counted, measured, or tied up. It cannot open sealed vessels, steal grain from a bushel (although it can falsify the weighing in the first place), and so forth. Many demons in Jewish lore have this limitation."
    }
    #tc86d71afc39b5c401bc887 ^"Protected Group" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t0fa5697338cf5051460713 ^"Demon Weakness"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 33
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The demon cannot act directly against a particular, reasonably common, group of people. It may not be able to affect children, or men with beards, or female Muslims. None of its Supernatural Powers work on this group, and if they face it in combat, it can only defend itself. A person who is not a member of the protected group is safe from the demon if he remains within a defined group of at least nine others who *are* protected from the demon. Likewise, two vulnerable people can hide within a group with a total size of twenty, and so forth."
    }
    #te0a70de7ed7f91ef0558ab ^"Running Water" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t0fa5697338cf5051460713 ^"Demon Weakness"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 33
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The demon cannot cross running water. This must be fresh water deriving directly from within the earth — spilled water from a jar will not hinder it."
    }
    #t170b6701cf169ee1f3d395 ^"Vulnerability" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t0fa5697338cf5051460713 ^"Demon Weakness"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 33
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A certain substance (see Abhorrent Material for appropriate examples) causes a Light Wound to the demon merely by touch. The more powerful the demon, the rarer this substance should be. Any weapons made of the material to which the demon is vulnerable inflict a Light Wound to the demon on a successful attack in addition to any damage inflicted as a result of the attack, even if the demon’s soak absorbs all the other damage. Light is a common Vulnerability of weak demons."
    }
    # The chapter's demons, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.
    #t187d89acfedc11a54c4815 ^"Adramelech, King of Fire" DEF {
        EXTENDS #t167900677b9e928b0cb39f ^"Demon"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Might Realm" STRING "Infernal" FIXED
            ^"Order" STRING "Prince of the False Gods"
            ^"Might" INTEGER 50
            ^"Form" STRING "Ignem"
            ^"Characteristics" DEF {
                ^"Intelligence" INTEGER 3
                ^"Perception" INTEGER 0
                ^"Presence" INTEGER 3
                ^"Communication" INTEGER 1
                ^"Strength" INTEGER 5
                ^"Stamina" INTEGER 5
                ^"Dexterity" INTEGER 4
                ^"Quickness" INTEGER 4
            }
            ^"Printed Size" STRING "0 (human), +2 (peacock)"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "3 (9 points)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Greater Immunity to Flame and Heat, Puissant Leadership, Piercing Gaze"
            ^"Reputations" LIST ["King of Hell 8 (Infernal)", "Kindler of the Hell Fires 5 (Infernal)"]
            ^"Hierarchy" INTEGER 9
            ^"Soak" INTEGER 9
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20)"
            ^"Weakness" STRING "Protected Group (Infants)"
            ^"Vis" STRING "10 pawns of Ignem, in feathers of the peacock"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "As a king, crowned in gold and robed in scarlet. His hair is made of living flames, his beard is made of smoke, and his eyes are glowing coals. He carries an immense sword. His constant companion and mount is a huge peacock, whose tail eyespots are glowing eyes of fire."
            ^"Source" STRING "Realms of Power: The Infernal"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 50
        }
        PERSONALITY_TRAITS {
            "Proud" +6
            "Regal" +6
            "Condescending" +3
        }
        COMBAT {
            "Great sword" INIT 6 ATTACK 18 DEFENSE 15 DAMAGE 14
        }
        ABILITIES {
            "Artes Liberales" SCORE 7 SPECIALTY "geometry"
            "Awareness" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "sinners"
            "Bargain" SCORE 8 SPECIALTY "pacts"
            "Brawl" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "kick"
            "Charm" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "innocent"
            "Folk Ken" SCORE 7 SPECIALTY "diabolists"
            "Great Weapon" SCORE 8 SPECIALTY "great sword"
            "Guile" SCORE 10 SPECIALTY "the proud"
            "Infernal Lore" SCORE 8 SPECIALTY "fire demons"
            "Intrigue" SCORE 8 SPECIALTY "the Pit"
            "Leadership" SCORE 12 BONUS 2 SPECIALTY "humans"
            "Philosophiae" SCORE 7 SPECIALTY "metaphysics"
            "Teaching" SCORE 6 SPECIALTY "academic abilities"
            "Theology" SCORE 8 SPECIALTY "nature of evil"
        }
        POWERS {
            #te40a2611516544b0965ac8 ^"King of Fire" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "variable points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "+3"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Ignem"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "Adramelech can create any Ignem-based effect, at a cost of 1 Might per two magnitudes. Ritual effects cost him twice as much, and an hour to summon up."
            }
            #t69b4dd6a26b998805089be ^"Regal Countenance" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "5 points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "0"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Mentem"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "When Adramelech issues an order, those succumbing to this Power are forced to obey it. The order must be terse, unambiguous, and involve a single, immediate action. For every additional point of Might expended on this Power, the demon can affect two more targets with the same order."
            }
            #tb934d2991c679e9492375f ^"Coagulation" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "5 points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "–1"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "See Chapter 4: Infernal Legions, Demonic Powers."
            }
            #t68d52a127ceff3b308b2c0 ^"Obsession" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "1 to 3 points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "–5"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Vim"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "Pride, Envy, Cruelty. See Chapter 4: Infernal Legions, Demonic Powers."
            }
            #t3a96a55645c2f03be52087 ^"Shroud the Stench of the Pit" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "variable points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "+3"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Vim"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "See Chapter 4: Infernal Legions, False Gods."
            }
            #td875763a42478e6d58c5f3 ^"The Wealth of Nations" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "3 points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "0"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Terram"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "See Chapter 4: Infernal Legions, False Gods."
            }
            #tb80c4c464a7a3665f5bf29 ^"His Master’s Voice" DEF {
                PROPERTIES {
                    ^"Cost" STRING "variable points"
                    ^"Initiative" STRING "+1"
                    ^"Form" STRING "Vim"
                }
                DESCRIPTION "See Chapter 4: Infernal Legions, False Gods."
            }
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Adramelech is a mighty demon, one of the most powerful in Hell. He is of ancient origin; he was among those who fell with Satan, and first lit the fires of Hell in an attempt to mimic the glorious light of Heaven. In olden times he was worshiped by the men of Tyre and Carthage as a god called Moloch. His devout worshipers sacrificed babies to him, for he has a special hatred of children. The infants were killed by placing them on the outstretched hands of Adramelech’s immense bronze idols, so that they fell into the fire which was lit below the statues. In modern times, he is seen on earth only upon the instigation of some diabolist. If anyone has the temerity to attack him physically, he can produce fire hot enough to melt steel and scorch flesh. He is not a particularly subtle demon, but he is not to be taken lightly."
    }
