    # The chapter's devices, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.
    #t6466c4994c6d59791037e7 ^"Control Spirit" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "the Circlet of the Primus"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Rego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Vim"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 55
            ^"Penetration" STRING "20"
            ^"Uses" STRING "unlimited uses per day"
            ^"Range" STRING "Arc"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 5, +4 Arc, +1 Conc; +10 unlimited uses, +5 item maintains concentration, +10 for Penetration Total of 20)."
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "Rego Vim 55 Pen: 20, unlimited uses per day R: Arc, D: Conc, T: Ind."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 44
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This power allows the wielder to command a single task of any spirit in her presence, or to whom the wielder has an Arcane Connection. The commands are issued mentally, and the circlet itself is inscribed with the names of (that is, Arcane Connections to) all of Fudarus’ servant spirits. Any spirit whose Might is less than the Penetration Total of the circlet can be affected by this power."
    }
    #t1101fd3064461a9749dc74 ^"Control Environment of Fudarus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "the Rod of the Primus"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Variable"
            ^"Form" STRING "Variable"
            ^"Penetration" STRING "0"
            ^"Uses" STRING "unlimited uses per day"
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Structure"
            ^"Effect Line" STRING "Variable Technique, Form, and Level Pen: 0, unlimited uses per day R: Touch, D: Conc, T: Structure"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 44
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The rod has six similar enchantments that use the same spell parameters, but have varying Arts and final levels. The rod can maintain any number of these effects simultaneously, but can only activate one per round.

• Vary light levels from total darkness to unbearable brightness. MuIg base 1, final level 25 • Vary temperature from below freezing to baking hot. MuIg base 1, final level 25 • Open archways or close portals between rooms. MuTe base 1, +1 stone, final level 30 • Create intense smells, either pleasant or putrid. CrIm base 1, final level 25 • Create noises, either soothing or clamoring. CrIm base 1, final level 25 • Change textures of furnishings to feel as soft as down or as sharp as thorns. MuIm base 1, final level 25 • (variable base, +1 Touch, +1 Conc, +3 Structure; +10 unlimited uses, +5 item maintains concentration)

The Circlet of the Primus commands the spiritual servants of the covenant. Although they can rarely be detected, every room has several invisible spirits within it that perform the simple, menial tasks of the covenant. The servants normally perform whatever task to which they were last set, and the wearer of the circlet is the only individual who can change the commands of a spirit. Prima Buliste currently wears the circlet."
    }
    # Iasper filius Adanos of House Tytalus (Chapter Four: Brittany, p45): one character, its stat lines verbatim fields.
    #t3f98e0fbd5abcfd0db35da ^"Iasper filius Adanos of House Tytalus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tffeed8bdd536ed47a1d64d ^"Exspectatio"]
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int +3, Per –1, Pre +2, Com 0, Str 0, Sta +2, Dex –1, Qik –2"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "26"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "0"
            ^"Warping Score" STRING "0 (4)"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "2 (6)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "The Gift; Hermetic Magus; Flexible Formulaic Magic; Affinity with Rego, Clear Thinker, Harnessed Magic, Magical Focus (Turmoil), Puissant Concentration, Puissant Terram, Self Confident; Chaotic Magic, Meddler; Close Family Ties, Incomprehensible, Weird Magic. House Virtue"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Argumentative +2, Self-Disciplined +2, Brave +1"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Fist: Init –2, Attack +1, Defense 0, Damage 0"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+2"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20), Dead (21+)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Artes Liberales 3 (literature), Brawl 2 (fist), Breton 3 (arguments), Concentration 2+2 (Rego), Finesse 2 (Terram), Etiquette 1 (politeness), French 5 (Norman), Latin 4 (Hermetic), Leadership 1 (brow-beating), Magic Lore 1 (earth spirits), Magic Theory 4 (Terram), Normandy Lore 1 (hostilities), Parma Magica 1 (Mentem), Penetration 1 (Terram), Philosophiae 1 (debating) Arts: Cr4, In 2, Mu 2, Pe 2, Re 10; An 2, Aq 6, Au 6, Co 3, He 0, Ig 3, Im 5, Me 5, Te 6+3, Vi 4"
            ^"Spells Known" STRING "Chaos of the Angry Waves (ReAq 30/+24) Confusion of the Insane Vibrations (ReIm 30/+22) Confusion of the Numbed Will (ReMe 15/+22) Crest of the Earth’s Wave (ReTe 20/+21) Panic of the Trembling Heart (CrMe 15/+11) Prying Eyes (InIm 5/+9) The Earth’s Carbuncle (ReTe (Mu) 15/+13) Wielding the Invisible Sling (ReTe 10/+21)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "A thin man with long shaggy black hair and an unshaven face. In contrast to his unkempt features, his clothing is always impeccably turned out."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 45
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Iasper filius Adanos of House Tytalus

Iasper is the youngest member of Exspectatio, having passed his Gauntlet just four years ago. He is a study in contrasts, since his magic is simultaneously tightly harnessed and unpredictable. He prides himself on his self-control, and yet has a natural affinity for turmoil and chaos, and delights in its execution. Given his master’s interests in Terram, he is fairly competent with this Art as well. Iasper is interested in reined chaos, which he believes is the route to self-understanding. Unlike many of his house, he provokes conflict beyond his capacity to control, seeing the vagaries of chance as a learning experience. There is no malice in his actions, although he rarely considers the implications of his actions for others."
    }
    # Korrigan (Chapter Four: Brittany, p38): one being, its stat lines verbatim fields.
    #t23d66551f365ec068339c8 ^"Korrigan" DEF {
        EXTENDS #taDz3ITq9fRoE374AgiL8VE4 ^"Creature"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Location" LIST [#t3936139d064f38314d5df8 ^"Brittany"]
            ^"Might Realm" STRING "Faerie" FIXED
            ^"Faerie Might" STRING "Typically 5–10; rarely 15 (Animal)"
            ^"Characteristics" DEF {
                ^"Intelligence" INTEGER -2
                ^"Perception" INTEGER 1
                ^"Presence" INTEGER -2
                ^"Communication" INTEGER 1
                ^"Strength" INTEGER -1
                ^"Stamina" INTEGER 3
                ^"Dexterity" INTEGER 2
                ^"Quickness" INTEGER 2
            }
            ^"Size" INTEGER -2
            ^"Age" STRING "n/a"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "0"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "None"
            ^"Reputations" LIST ["Dangerous 3 (local)", "Tireless dancers 1 (local)", "Magicians 1 (local)"]
            ^"Soak" INTEGER 3
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "n/a"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–3), –3 (4–6), -5 (7–9), Incapacitated (10–12), Dead (13+)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Area Lore 3 (paths), Athletics 5 (dancing), Awareness 4 (gold, silver), Brawl 2 (claws), Guile 1 (bargaining), Speak Breton 4 (commands), Stealth 4 (hiding), Single Weapon 2 (club), Thrown Weapon 2 (stones) Powers (not all have this): Human Form, 5 points, Init 2, Corpus: The more powerful korrigan can assume the form of a beautiful young woman. The transformation lasts for one hour, or until the same amount of Might is expended to reverse it. In human form, the following changes apply: Characteristics (human form): Int –2, Per +1, Pre +2, Com +1, Str –1, Sta 0, Dex 0, Qik –1; Size (human form): 0 Club: Init +0, Attack +2, Defense +0, Damage +2 Stone (thrown): Init -1, Attack +3, Defense +1, Damage +1"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Usually none."
            ^"Natural Weapons" STRING "Claws: Init -1, Attack +2, Defense +3, Damage +2."
            ^"Encumberance" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Vis" STRING "1 pawn of Animal vis in hooves"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "A hunchbacked manikin about three feet tall with cat’s claws on its hands and goat’s hooves for feet."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 38
        }
        PERSONALITY_TRAITS {
            "Avaricious" +2
            "Capricious" +2
            "Short-tempered" +2
        }
        COMBAT {
            "Claws" INIT 1 ATTACK 7 DEFENSE 8 DAMAGE 1
            " Club" INIT 3 ATTACK 6 DEFENSE 5 DAMAGE 2
            " Stone (thrown)" INIT 2 ATTACK 5 DEFENSE 4 DAMAGE 1
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Anyone attempting to collect vis or investigate the mysteries of the forest will have to contend with the korrigan (singular: korred). A korred is a hunchbacked manikin about three feet tall with cat’s claws on its hands and goat’s hooves for feet; with the expenditure of Might, it may take on the form of a beautiful young woman. They are known as dancers and magicians. Since their queen, Viviane, lost interest in the Brocéliande forest and them, the korrigan in this region have become very dangerous. Elsewhere, they may live in forests, caves, or dolmens, where they collect valuable objects. They administer severe punishments to those who annoy them, but periodically give rewards from their treasures. In some places, they like to dance in a circle holding hands under the moonlight at a crossroads and, if they are in a good mood, invite all who pass to join them. Those who accept may be given a gift, but those who refuse are punished.

These statistics apply to the korrigan of Brocéliande. Those encountered in other parts of Brittany are less dangerous; they are more interested in dancing and riches, though still unpredictable and short-tempered."
    }
    # Kybella of House Tytalus (Chapter Four: Brittany, p45): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.
    #t0a2a5c56e0dd2cdb314b31 ^"Kybella of House Tytalus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tffeed8bdd536ed47a1d64d ^"Exspectatio"]
            ^"Age" STRING "68 (Apparent age 48)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Loyal to Buliste +3, Suspicious +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 45
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A leading member of the Titanoi, House Tytalus’s cult of theurgists (see *Houses of Hermes: Societates*, House Tytalus). She is responsible for maintaining the enchantments that hold Fudarus’s spirits in check, and is a close friend of Prima Buliste. She specializes in genii loci, and carefully inspects every place she stays for evidence of such spirits. Kybella’s current interests revolve around her involvement of the Cabal of the Laden Cart (see Sagas: Plots of House Tytalus)."
    }
    # Nain (Chapter Four: Brittany, p48): one being, its stat lines verbatim fields.
