    # David ben David (Chapter Twelve: Curse of the Rhine Gorge, p131): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.
    #t95f9794804234447ab42cd ^"David ben David" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int +2, Per 0, Pre 0, Com +2, Str 0, Sta +1, Dex 0, Qik 0"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "30 (30)"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "None"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Merchant; Wealthy; Educated, Puissant Bargain, Social Contacts, Well-Traveled; Pious, Outsider; Judged Unfairly"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Devout Jew +3, Honest +2, Insensitive to Insults +2"
            ^"Reputations" STRING "Jew 3 (Local)"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Dodging: Init 0, Attack n/a, Defense 0, Damage n/a"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+1"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, -1, -3, -5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "-1 (1-5), -3 (6-10), -5 (11-15), Incapacitated (16-20)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Aramaic 3 (Torah), Animal Handling 2 (horses), Artes Liberales 3 (accounts), Awareness 2 (faulty goods), Bargain 5+2 (luxuries), Bavarian Lore 2 (towns), Carouse 2 (amongst Jews), Charm 2 (gaining trust), Civil and Canon Law 3 (regarding merchants), Etiquette 2 (gentlemen), Folk Ken 3 (empathizing), French 2 (trading), Guile 2 (perceiving cheats), High German 6 (Yiddish), Intrigue 3 (merchants), Italian 2 (trading), Latin 3 (bargaining), Leadership 1 (amongst Jews), Low German 2 (trading), Medicine 2 (infected wounds), Philosophiae 2 (debate), Profession: Merchant 4 (luxury goods), Profession: Ship’s Captain 2 (on the Rhine), Rhine Lore 3 (towns), Ride 1 (good roads), Swabian Lore 2 (towns), Swim 2 (rivers), Teaching 2 (Academic Abilities), Theology: Jewish 3 (duties)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Plain clothing befitting a merchant, bearing the wheel symbol of Jewdom, skull cap."
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Of average height, David is unmistakably Jewish, both through physiognomy and through cultural symbols. He wears his black hair short, with two long curly braids in front of each ear. When appropriate he dons the skull cap and/or prayer shawl, unashamed to be seen in public with these clear symbols of his religion. He dresses moderately, not flaunting his wealth."
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 131
        }
        DESCRIPTION "David ben David is a wealthy merchant from an even wealthier Jewish family, who plies his trade between Trier, Koblenz, Bingen, and Mainz. His family has operated in this region for years, and as a child he traveled far and wide with his father and uncles, learning all about the Rhine, its tributaries, and its trade. When he reached thirteen, he entered the famous Jewish academy at Mainz and learned both his Aramaic and Latin letters, as well as scholarly pursuits such as (Jewish) Theology, Artes Liberales, and Medicine. When his father died ten years ago he returned to Trier to take over the business, which also involved taking a wife, Sophie. They have yet to have any children.

David’s biggest stumbling block is his religion. He is a devout Jew, and proudly wears the patch of cloth identifying him as such (see Chapter 5: The Rhine, Jews in the Holy Roman Empire), despite it being a symbol of the Christian oppression of his people. He refuses to compromise his religious devotion to make his life easier, as so many other fellow Jews have. Despite suspicion and outright hatred from his Christian competitors, David has maintained a level head and a very thick hide. Given his age, education, and convictions, it will not be long before he is asked to become a rabbi by his community, where his kindness is greatly respected."
    }
    # The chapter's devices, structured; each DESCRIPTION the source's text, verbatim.
    #td67001a168bf1b8e558c06 ^"Recognize Your Master" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "The Door of Deimos"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Corpus"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 5
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Mom"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 4, +1 Touch)"
            ^"Final Level" STRING "8"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "InCo 5, R:Touch, D:Mom, T:Ind"
            ^"Location" LIST [#tf4daa04d297b09116481a4 ^"The Sanctum of Arliandus"]
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 132
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This is an iron door, with faces and skulls embossed onto its surface and highlighted in inlaid lead and silver. Arliandus named it after the son of Ares, whose name meant “Terror.” The door is not locked, but has a complex latch requiring putting one’s hand inside the mouth of a leering face and twisting the catch. The door is also invested with the following effects:

A compartment on the inside of the door holds an arcane connection (currently to the long-dead Arliandus). If the arcane connection matches the person touching the door, then nothing happens. If it does not match, or the toucher successfully resisted the effect (it has a Penetration Total of 0), then the second effect is triggered. The toucher may choose not to resist this effect if he knows it exists. This effect is triggered even if the door is not touched with bare flesh. Operates 6 times per day (+3 levels)."
    }
    #t4fde2dcf2285130f5b7989 ^"Repel the Intruder" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "The Door of Deimos"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Mentem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 15
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 4, +1 Touch, +2 Sun)"
            ^"Final Level" STRING "43"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "CrMe 15, R:Touch, D:Sun, T:Ind"
            ^"Location" LIST [#tf4daa04d297b09116481a4 ^"The Sanctum of Arliandus"]
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 132
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This effect is triggered by the first effect (+3 levels). Anyone affected must make an Intelligence roll against an Ease Factor of 12 or flee in terror. Operates 6 times per day (+3 levels), has a Penetration Total of 22 (+11 levels)."
    }
    #t41800cf5fd701dbcadce37 ^"Lamp without Flame" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "The Crystal of a Hundred Candles"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Creo"
            ^"Form" STRING "Ignem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 10
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 4, +1 Touch, +1 Conc)"
            ^"Final Level" STRING "23"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "CrIg 10, R:Touch, D:Conc, T:Ind"
            ^"Location" LIST [#tf4daa04d297b09116481a4 ^"The Sanctum of Arliandus"]
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 132
        }
        DESCRIPTION "As the door opens, a small crystal embedded in the ceiling blooms into light, illuminating the whole chamber.

Operates 24 times per day (+5 levels), item maintains concentration (+5 levels), environmental trigger (+3 levels)."
    }
    #t73da1e888a09a1f04db599 ^"Depiction of the Waking Dream" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Part Of" STRING "The Mirror of Dreams"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Intellego"
            ^"Form" STRING "Mentem"
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Creo, Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 35
            ^"Range" STRING "Eye"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Conc"
            ^"Target" STRING "Ind"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 25, +1 Eye, +1 Conc)"
            ^"Final Level" STRING "45"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "InCrMeIm 35, R:Eye, D:Conc, T:Ind"
            ^"Location" LIST [#tf4daa04d297b09116481a4 ^"The Sanctum of Arliandus"]
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 132
        }
        DESCRIPTION "An ornate, gold-framed mirror is surrounded by a set of elaborate smaller mirror fragments — a willing subject who stares into it will see his own thoughts visualized before his eyes. This assists greatly with certain types of lab work; +3 may be added to any Lab Total involving Mentem. However, use of the Mirror is unsettling and tends to disturb the user’s dreams; 1 Warping Point is gained for each season of use (this is due to it being a Powerful Mystical Effect). It also counts as a continuous effect for calculating yearly gain of Warping Points.

The thoughts of the subject become visible as images surrounding his head in a mirror. The workings of Mentem spells can thus be analyzed quite precisely. Unlimited uses (+10 levels)."
    }
    #t0ab09594b801539762cc07 ^"Vision of the Haunting Spirits (Guardians of the Forests)" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tYiQyfVMioMALqPGoncvpTfY ^"Enchanted Device"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Printed Name" STRING "Vision of the Haunting Spirits"
            ^"Part Of" STRING "The Trumpet of Ghostly Summoning"
            ^"Technique" STRING "Muto"
            ^"Form" STRING "Mentem"
            ^"Requisite" STRING "Imaginem"
            ^"Level" INTEGER 40
            ^"Range" STRING "Touch"
            ^"Duration" STRING "Sun"
            ^"Target" STRING "Room"
            ^"Effect Design" STRING "(Base 15, +1 Touch, +2 Sun, +2 Room)"
            ^"Final Level" STRING "41"
            ^"Printed Effect Line" STRING "MuMeIm 40, R:Touch, D:Sun, T:Room"
            ^"Location" LIST [#tf4daa04d297b09116481a4 ^"The Sanctum of Arliandus"]
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 132
        }
        DESCRIPTION "A small silver trumpet, when blown, summons forth any ghosts or spirits in the area and renders them visible.

Operates twice per day (+1 level)."
    }
    # Hilda (Chapter Twelve: Curse of the Rhine Gorge, p117): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.
    #tb75979318968ae64897005 ^"Hilda" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int 0, Per 0, Pre –1, Com +1, Str +4, Sta +2, Dex +1, Qik –2"
            ^"Size" STRING "+1"
            ^"Age" STRING "28"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "0"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Custos; Great Strength, Puissant Single Weapon; Covenant Upbringing, Obese, Oversensitive (to disrespect)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Brave +3, Loyal to Magi +3, Tolerant –3"
            ^"Reputations" STRING "None"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Mace and heater shield: Init –1, Attack +13, Defense +10, Damage +12 Mace: Init –1, Attack +12, Defense +6, Damage +12 Short bow: Init –4, Attack +7, Defense +1, Damage +10 Pole axe: Init –1, Attack +9, Defense +1, Damage +15 Dagger: Init –2, Attack +7, Defense +2, Damage +7 Fist: Init –2, Attack +5, Defense +2, Damage +4 Grapple: Init –2, Attack +6, Defense +3, Damage +4"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+9"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1-6), –3 (7-12), –5 (13-18), Incapacitated (19-24)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Athletics 2 (endurance), Awareness 3 (ambushes), Bows 2 (short bow), Brawl 4 (grappling), Carouse 1 (drinking quantity), Folk Ken 2 (peasants), High German 5 (orders), Great Weapon 2 (pole axe), Latin 3 (making reports), Leadership 5 (grogs), Music 1 (singing loudly), Order of Hermes Lore 2 (Fengheld), Single Weapon 6+2 (mace and heater shield), Teaching 2 (Martial Abilities)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Full metal scale armor, mace, heater shield. Hilda also carries a pole axe and a short bow, and a standard traveler’s kit with any number of useful tools."
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "0 (4)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Hilda is an immense woman, both in height and girth. She wears her blonde hair short, to suit her helmet more comfortably, and has piercing blue eyes. Her armor, specially made for her, has the appearance of being made by a cooper rather than an armorer."
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 117
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Hilda is a covenant grog, born and bred at Fengheld. Given this upbringing she finds nothing unusual about a woman being a warrior, and is constantly surprised that the “mundanes” have such an issue with this. She is prime leadership material, and will whip any unformed grogs into military shape with ease. She is also competent at her main job — breaking heads — and Fengheld valued her highly, making the gift of her to young magi all the more valuable. She has a forceful personality and brooks no disobedience, disrespect, or laziness, which tends to make her less popular with the other grogs — but as she sees it, she is not out to make any friends."
    }
