            ^"Page" INTEGER 117
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Syagricus is the oddest Jerbiton member of the covenant, both in temperament and physically. He is a genuine hermaphrodite and seems quite proud of it. He dresses to accentuate both his male and female gender, wearing a full beard and a dress that accentuates his bust. His sexual nature is inexplicable but medically proven, and Syagricus sees his true nature as beautiful and refuses to hide it. His sodales are very accepting of his nature, but would prefer he didn’t mention it as much as he does.

Syagricus happily imbibes his Longevity Ritual, which is a daily mixture of specially prepared herbs and powders drunk at noon, and is hale and hearty. Interested in art, etiquette, and a pleasant life, much like his sodales, he is more determined to regain the covenant’s objects of art lost when they fled Constantinople than in continuing a hedonistic lifestyle. Syagricus has joined Valnastium’s league of New Iconophiles (*Houses of Hermes: Soceitates*, page 54), and travels to Constantinople at least once a year to search for the lost pieces of art.

Syagricus’ apprentice, Pancratius, is due to be gauntleted in 1221, and hopes to receive the honor at the upcoming Tribunal. Pancratius will likely join Moero’s Garden as a full member, and Trasaric and Helladius hope that he will side with them in assisting the emperor, tipping the vote in their favor."
    }
    # Ziper of House Tytalus (Chapter Eight: Anatolia, p117): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.
    #tfc8679e7e7c84175091132 ^"Ziper of House Tytalus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t971f29fc8b8b7dfe6c00c7 ^"Moero’s Garden"]
            ^"Age" STRING "129 (Apparent Age: 65)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Conniving +3, Obsequious +3, Busybody +2"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 117
        }
        DESCRIPTION "The oldest magus at Moero’s Garden, Ziper joined after its relocation to Nicaea. He usually dresses in white robes and a red overlying toga. He is stooped and wrinkled and completely bald. His appearance is deceiving, for while he looks venerable, he has the energy and acumen of a youth.

Ziper feels that the covenant needs new members, that its size is a detriment to its standing in the Tribunal. He has proposed that Nanno and Ampelius be accepted into the covenant as members of House Jerbiton. While not magi, they can effect minor enchantments within their creations. Proximios of House Mercere (see The Covenant of Alexandria, earlier) supports his position, citing how beneficial his House of unGifted people is to the Order, and theorizing that unGifted members in House Jerbiton would only contribute to its success. The other members, apart from Syagricus, are horrified at this proposal, not because Nanno and Ampelius are unGifted, but because they are craftsmen! Both artisans, Nanno more so than Ampelius, think the life of a magus must be wonderful, and threaten to travel to Delos and ask the Tribunal as a whole for membership."
    }
    # Character Guide: A Sibyl (Chapter Nine: The Magical Landscape, p121): one being, its printed stat lines verbatim fields.
    #t84e024eefa2f0f3d3aa412 ^"Character Guide: A Sibyl" DEF {
        EXTENDS #taDz3ITq9fRoE374AgiL8VE4 ^"Creature"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Might Realm" STRING "Magic" FIXED
            ^"Magic Might" STRING "25+ (Mentem)"
            ^"Season" STRING "Winter"
            ^"Characteristics" DEF {
                ^"Intelligence" INTEGER 5
                ^"Perception" INTEGER 6
                ^"Presence" INTEGER 0
                ^"Communication" INTEGER 1
                ^"Strength" INTEGER -1
                ^"Stamina" INTEGER 0
                ^"Dexterity" INTEGER -1
                ^"Quickness" INTEGER -1
            }
            ^"Size" INTEGER 0
            ^"Age" STRING "n/a (varies)"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "2 (6)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Magic Human, Magical Master; Famous, Self Confident; Meddler; Ability Block (Martial Abilities), Visions"
            ^"Magical Qualities and Inferiorities" STRING "Divination & Augury (see The Mysteries Revised Edition, Chapter 7), Improved Perception, Natural Appearance; Improved Abilities x 3, Mentem Resistance, Minor Virtue (additional Divination methods) x5, Minor Virtue (Great Intelligence) x2, Minor Virtue (Great Perception) x2, Minor Virtue (Improved Characteristics), Minor Virtue (Premonitions), Minor Virtue (Puissant Divination)"
            ^"Reputations" LIST ["Prophetess 4 (Local)"]
            ^"Soak" INTEGER 0
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20), Dead (21+)"
            ^"Vis" STRING "5 pawns of Mentem vis, in tools of divination"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Each sibyl appears as a woman native to the area; some appear to be young maidens, whereas others appear as haggard crones. They wear flimsy veils across their faces, or else a blindfold."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 121
        }
        PERSONALITY_TRAITS {
            "Enigmatic" +6
            "Meddlesome" +3
            "Brave" +1
        }
        COMBAT {
            "Unarmed Defense" INIT -1 DEFENSE -1
        }
        ABILITIES {
            "Classical Greek" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "prophetic pronouncement"
            "[Area A] Lore" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "varies"
            "[Area B] Lore" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "varies"
            "[Area C] Lore" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "varies"
            "Artes Liberales" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "scribing riddles"
            "Divination" SCORE 10 BONUS 2 SPECIALTY "varies"
            "Faerie Lore" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "prophecy"
            "Guile" SCORE 1 SPECIALTY "under duress"
            "Intrigue" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "local politics"
            "Latin" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "declamations"
            "Living Language" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "local dialect"
            "Magic Lore" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "prophecy"
            "Mentem Resistance" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "mind-reading"
            "[Organization A] Lore" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "varies"
            "[Organization B] Lore" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "varies"
            "Penetration" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "Divination"
            "Philosophiae" SCORE 4 SPECIALTY "natural philosophy"
            "Premonitions" SCORE 5 SPECIALTY "nations"
            "Teaching" SCORE 3 SPECIALTY "Area Lore"
        }
        DESCRIPTION "This character guide follows the rules for Magic Characters (see *Realms of Power: Magic*, pages 29–54), and describes the basic minimum game statistics of a sibyl. However, there is plenty of room for customization; the sibyl has only 5 points of Virtues and Flaws, and most sibyls have a Magic Might greater that 25, allowing room for some overtly magical powers rather than relying on Divination, Premonitions, and a vast knowledge of diverse subjects. The sibyl’s Enigmatic Personality Trait is an Essential Trait; magical effects to make her speak clearly mysteriously fail. Some sibyls might be Transformed Humans rather than Magic Humans."
    }
